# Dashboard Layout

Basic view logic for dashboard and LC tab pages. Follow when adding or changing dashboard sections.

## Page stack (`dashboard-main`, `lc-page`)

- Vertical stack only — no `mt-auto` on sections (avoids empty space when content is short).
- Consistent rhythm: `gap-4` (16px) on mobile, `gap-6` (24px) from `sm:` up.
- Every section: `w-full min-w-0` so cards fill the content area and shrink correctly.

## Summary card grid (`dashboard-summary-cards`)

Used on Dashboard (Required Documents + Compliance) and LC tab insight cards.

| Viewport | Layout |
|----------|--------|
| &lt; md (768px) | Single column — cards full width, stacked |
| md+ | Two equal columns — `grid-cols-2`, same gap as page stack |

- Cards use `h-full flex flex-col` so paired cards match height.
- Card body uses `flex-1` so inner content fills the card.
- Tables live inside `ui-table-wrap` for horizontal scroll; never force card overflow.

## Compliance report card

- Below `md`: metrics above chart (stacked).
- `md+`: row layout — metrics ~75%, chart ~25%.
- Footer CTA stays at the bottom of the card via flex column on `.dashboard-compliance-report`.

## Section order (Dashboard)

1. Recent LC table (full width)
2. Summary card grid (2 columns from md)
3. How it works (full width)

## Breakpoints to verify

320px, 768px, 1024px, 1280px — especially split-screen / narrowed laptop widths.
